description:
You are tasked with designing a verilog module that implements a 2-to-1 multiplexer using the following interface:
```
module mux_2to1 (
    input a,
    input b,
    input sel,
    output out
);
```
The module should select `a` or `b` as the output based on the value of `sel`. If `sel` is `0`, then `a` should be the output. If `sel` is `1`, then `b` should be the output.

You may use any verilog constructs to implement the multiplexer. Your module should have the following properties:
- It should be synthesizable
- It should not use any latches or tri-state buffers
- It should pass the provided testbench

```
module testbench;

    reg a, b, sel;
    wire out;

    mux_2to1 dut (
        .a(a),
        .b(b),
        .sel(sel),
        .out(out)
    );

    initial begin
        $display("a b sel | out");
        $monitor("%b %b %b | %b", a, b, sel, out);

        a = 0; b = 0; sel = 0;
        #10;
        if (out !== 0) $error("Test failed");

        a = 1; b = 0; sel = 0;
        #10;
        if (out !== 1) $error("Test failed");

        a = 0; b = 1; sel = 0;
        #10;
        if (out !== 0) $error("Test failed");

        a = 1; b = 1; sel = 0;
        #10;
        if (out !== 1) $error("Test failed");

        a = 0; b = 0; sel = 1;
        #10;
        if (out !== 0) $error("Test failed");

        a = 1; b = 0; sel = 1;
        #10;
        if (out !== 0) $error("Test failed");

        a = 0; b = 1; sel = 1;
        #10;
        if (out !== 1) $error("Test failed");

        a = 1; b = 1; sel = 1;
        #10;
        if (out !== 1) $error("Test failed");

        $display("All tests passed");
        $finish;
    end

endmodule
```

